## Recovery Contract

- A missing, changed, invalid, or escaping reference fails before mutation with a controlled
  preparation error.
- Exhausted retrieval budget returns explicit insufficient-context evidence; it never invents a
  complete plan.
- Possible post-mutation execution failures retain the existing reconciliation-required and
  no-replay behavior.
- Failed platform, CI, release, or production evidence leaves the owning outcome chain open.

## Program Constraints

- No unrestricted shell, network, parent workspace access, mutable reference, or new hosted
  retrieval service.
- No increase to the global inline-context cap as the primary solution.
- Telemetry records identity, digest, counts, byte totals, and result categories, never retrieved
  source content.
- Work2 modifies development lanes only; Work5 publication follows the complete configured route.

## Verification Strategy

- Unit-test manifest determinism, digest validation, path normalization, symlink and traversal
  refusal, range bounds, byte budgets, cumulative budgets, evidence, and fallback.
- Exercise a preparation whose declared context is larger than the inline ceiling but whose actual
  bounded reads succeed.
- Run full repository validation, development web checks, clean and upgraded disposable Linux and
  Windows qualification, exact-SHA CI, release provenance, every production lane, and immediate
  dashboard convergence.
